      "content": "While caffeine can indeed help increase focus, it also has side effects, especially in higher dosages. Consuming two 200mg caffeine pills could significantly increase your intake, potentially leading to jitteriness, digestive issues, and impaired sleep, which could negatively impact your exam performance. It's also important to note that you are taking medication for ADHD, and altering this could interfere with its efficacy or cause your body to build a tolerance and dependence. Consult with your healthcare provider before making any changes to your routine. They can offer personalized advice considering your medical history and needs.",
